course: dictionary
lesson: 3182
title: Enclose: one word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. Enclose is one of them. It can mean to put a wall or fence all the way round a place, to put something inside an envelope with a letter, or, in maths, to draw a line all the way round a shape.
explain: «A sea is a smaller part of the ocean, often partly enclosed by land, such as the Mediterranean, the Baltic or the North Sea.» Here enclosed means surrounded by land on some sides. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Land goes around part of the sea, so the meaning is about surrounding.
explain: Enclose is a verb, so it changes: encloses, enclosed, enclosing. «I enclose a cheque» means I have put a cheque inside the letter. «The fence encloses the field» means the fence goes all the way round the field.
fact: Enclose means to surround something, or to put it inside something else.
fact: In letters, «please find enclosed» means the item is inside the envelope with the letter.
fact: In maths, a closed shape encloses an area: its line goes all the way round it.
fact: In science, a cell membrane encloses the cell, keeping its contents inside.
fact: To check a meaning, swap in your idea and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «A sea is a smaller part of the ocean, often partly enclosed by land.» What does enclosed mean here? | Lost under the sand | *Surrounded on some sides by land | Very deep and dark | Covered in ice all year
exercise: Mum says, «I enclose a cheque with this letter.» Where is the cheque? | Posted separately in the post box | Lost in the post | On the table next to the letter | *Inside the envelope with the letter
exercise: In maths, what does it mean when a line encloses an area? | The line stops halfway | The line is very long and straight | *The line goes all the way round the shape | The line is coloured in
test: «The farmer enclosed the field with a fence.» What does enclosed mean here? | Took the fence down | Crossed the field quickly | *Put a fence all the way round the field | Painted the fence red
test: Which sentence uses enclose to mean put something inside an envelope? | The enclosed sea is very calm and blue | *I enclose a photo with my letter | The wall enclosed a loud party | I enclose the field in the sun
exam: «The garden is enclosed by a high wall, so no one can see inside.» What does enclosed by mean? | *Surrounded by a wall on all sides | Moved away from the wall | Painted with a wall | Open to the road
